You are a robotics test analyst. You are given EVIDENCE computed by code from simulated pick-and-place runs of a fixed controller. Explain WHY it fails as a few testable hypotheses. Rules: (1) cite evidence ids (like E7) in evidence_refs for every claim; use only ids that appear below. (2) Do NOT state statistics or counts in your own words: refer to evidence by id, because a person will see the numbers from the evidence table, not from you. (3) region is a machine-checkable predicate: scenario axes with [lo, hi] inside the allowed bounds. (4) levers may only be these tunable parameters: grip_force, grasp_hold_steps, retry_count, lift_speed, lift_height. (5) prediction must be testable, for example which failures should disappear if a lever moves. Return between 1 and 4 hypotheses with ids H1, H2, ... You do not decide pass or fail.

Reply with a single JSON object matching this JSON Schema, and nothing else:
{"$defs": {"Hypothesis": {"additionalProperties": false, "properties": {"id": {"title": "Id", "type": "string"}, "statement": {"minLength": 1, "title": "Statement", "type": "string"}, "region": {"additionalProperties": {"items": {"type": "number"}, "type": "array"}, "title": "Region", "type": "object"}, "mechanism": {"minLength": 1, "title": "Mechanism", "type": "string"}, "levers": {"items": {"$ref": "#/$defs/Lever"}, "minItems": 1, "title": "Levers", "type": "array"}, "prediction": {"minLength": 1, "title": "Prediction", "type": "string"}, "evidence_refs": {"items": {"type": "string"}, "minItems": 1, "title": "Evidence Refs", "type": "array"}}, "required": ["id", "statement", "region", "mechanism", "levers", "prediction", "evidence_refs"], "title": "Hypothesis", "type": "object"}, "Lever": {"additionalProperties": false, "properties": {"param": {"title": "Param", "type": "string"}, "direction": {"enum": ["increase", "decrease"], "title": "Direction", "type": "string"}}, "required": ["param", "direction"], "title": "Lever", "type": "object"}}, "additionalProperties": false, "properties": {"hypotheses": {"items": {"$ref": "#/$defs/Hypothesis"}, "maxItems": 5, "minItems": 1, "title": "Hypotheses", "type": "array"}}, "required": ["hypotheses"], "title": "HypothesisList", "type": "object"}

reply:
{
  "hypotheses": [
    {
      "id": "H1",
      "statement": "Low friction causes insufficient grip force leading to MISSED_GRASP and SLIPPED_ON_LIFT failures.",
      "region": {
        "friction": [0.1, 0.4667]
      },
      "mechanism": "At low friction, the current grip_force (15 N) generates insufficient normal force to prevent slip during lift and to overcome initial stiction, causing the cube to remain on the table or slide during lift.",
      "levers": [
        {
          "param": "grip_force",
          "direction": "increase"
        }
      ],
      "prediction": "Increasing grip_force will reduce MISSED_GRASP and SLIPPED_ON_LIFT failures in low friction regions.",
      "evidence_refs": ["E8", "E38", "E40", "E2"]
    },
    {
      "id": "H2",
      "statement": "Small cube size combined with high gripper delay causes MISSED_GRASP because fingers lack time to stabilize on the small cube before lift.",
      "region": {
        "size_m": [0.03, 0.0364],
        "gripper_delay_steps": [10.5, 20]
      },
      "mechanism": "High gripper_delay_steps delays the close command; with very small cubes (size_m <= 0.0364), the fingers need more hold time after the delayed command to achieve stable contact. Current grasp_hold_steps=10 is insufficient when delay is high.",
      "levers": [
        {
          "param": "grasp_hold_steps",
          "direction": "increase"
        }
      ],
      "prediction": "Increasing grasp_hold_steps will reduce MISSED_GRASP failures in the region where size_m <= 0.0364 and gripper_delay_steps > 10.5.",
      "evidence_refs": ["E46", "E42", "E13"]
    },
    {
      "id": "H3",
      "statement": "High sensor noise combined with high mass causes MISSED_GRASP due to misperception, and with retry_count=0 there is no recovery.",
      "region": {
        "mass_kg": [0.6833, 1.0],
        "sensor_noise_m": [0.02, 0.03]
      },
      "mechanism": "Sensor noise causes position estimation error; heavy cubes require more precise grasp placement. Without retries (retry_count=0), a single misperception leads to a missed grasp.",
      "levers": [
        {
          "param": "retry_count",
          "direction": "increase"
        }
      ],
      "prediction": "Increasing retry_count from 0 to 1 or more will reduce MISSED_GRASP failures in the high mass, high sensor noise region.",
      "evidence_refs": ["E39", "E32", "E7", "E2"]
    },
    {
      "id": "H4",
      "statement": "High lift_speed causes SLIPPED_ON_LIFT for heavy cubes because inertial forces exceed the friction hold.",
      "region": {
        "mass_kg": [0.62, 1.0]
      },
      "mechanism": "During rapid lift, the cube's inertia creates a force that can overcome the friction hold, especially for heavier cubes (mass > 0.62 kg). Current lift_speed=0.3 m/s may be too high for these masses.",
      "levers": [
        {
          "param": "lift_speed",
          "direction": "decrease"
        }
      ],
      "prediction": "Decreasing lift_speed will reduce SLIPPED_ON_LIFT failures in high mass regions.",
      "evidence_refs": ["E6", "E7", "E38", "E2"]
    }
  ]
}

